    },
    {
      "title": "Accommodation",
      "value": "<p>A range of accommodation options is available to students on and off campus. Many first-year students choose to reside on campus in traditional shared accommodation with communal living areas. Suite-style accommodation is another option often chosen by second or third-year students as it allows for a more independent living arrangement, including bathrooms and kitchens.</p><p>The Wellness Housing program was created to provide a substance-free living environment for students who prefer to live a more clean lifestyle. The university also provides resources and advice on off-campus housing options in the nearby area, with students well-positioned to take advantage of the university's partnerships with nearby apartments. Due to its leafy green campus and how accessible nearby buildings are, 90% of students live on campus.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sports",
      "value": "<p>The Drew Athletics and Recreation Center provides programs for the university community to stay active, but team sports are also beloved. From cardio equipment to the Campus Recreation hosting the Drew Olympics, sports and fitness is well-catered to on campus. Performance opportunities come from the Dorothy Young Center for the Arts, Concert Hall and the Simon Forum and Athletic Center.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Lab",
      "value": "<p>Specialized laboratories in chemistry, biology, psychology and others were installed for students to access the necessary equipment for their course easily. It also allows for research possibilities to be realized.</p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Library",
      "value": "<p>The Rose Memorial Library and Methodist Library are the two main libraries on campus that provide access to over one million print and electronic resources. </p>",
      "image": null,
      "highlightType": "General"
    },
    {
      "title": "Student Life",
      "value": "<p>The community on campus is close-knit and welcoming to everybody, with over 60 organizations available for students to get involved in leisure activities with like-minded people. From sports to academia, there are people with a shared passion for meeting at Drew University. Dining options cater to a range of dietary needs and preferences, so students only have to embark on a short and scenic walk to find a proper bite to eat. The 186-acre campus is wooded, so the campus is aesthetically pleasing, and many students study outdoors in sunny weather.</p><p>The college town is ranked as the 3rd safest in the whole of the USA and the safest in New Jersey. Presidents and noted speakers often visit the university, and a mixture of academic and cultural events occur throughout the year. The campus is also ideally located close to New York City, so students get a mix of a leafy suburban feel and a thriving city.</p>",
